	    Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX <= Old_index, "IndexOf(x) is larger than index.");
	    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("msg0", "assertion - New_arrListIndexOfX <= Old_index");

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ New_arrListLastIndexOfX is equal to New_arrListIndexOfX
	    Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListIndexOfX, "LastIndexOf(x) is not same as IndexOf(x).");
	    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("msg1", "assertion - New_arrListLastIndexOfX == New_arrListIndexOfX");

	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ New_arrListContainsX is TRUE
	    Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == true, "Contains(x) is not true after inserting.");
	    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("msg2", "assertion - New_arrListContainsX == true");

	    PexAssume.True(!arrList.Contains('x'));

            // a loop invariant that  @@@ arrList.Contains(x) is TRUE and (foreach int i in arrList { Assert.IsTrue(i == x)})
	    PexAssume.True(arrList.Contains(x));
	    foreach (int i in arrList) {
		    PexObserve.ValueForViewing("i", i);
		    Assert.IsTrue(i == x);
	    }
	}
    }
}

```


For this specific test, an input sequence x and an insertion point index are taken as assumptions. The code then performs an insertion operation on ArrayList arrList at index index with value x. Post-condition observations and assertions are then performed to check the state of ArrayList after insertion.

ArrayList.Test names the test as PUT_InsertContract (PUT is an abbreviation for "Put" which is the standard name for a method corresponding to the HTTP PUT command). The test is also tagged with [PexAssumeUnderTest], which tells PexOS to consider this test as the potential state under test (SUT), especially since it directly interacts with ArrayList and has multiple operations to check its behaviour. Please note that PexAssumeUnderTest only works with non-static methods in the test class.

The test consists of multiple assertions that confirm the current state of ArrayList after the insertion operation. Assertions verify that:

- ArrayList Count increases by one upon insertion (New_arrList_Count == Old_arrList_Count + 1)
- IndexOf(x) is not larger than the insertion point (New_arrList_IndexOf_x <= Old_index)
- LastIndexOf(x) == IndexOf(x) after the insertion (New_arrList_LastIndexOf_x == New_arrListIndexOf_x)
- Contains(x) becomes TRUE after insertion (New_arrList_contains_x == TRUE)
- If x is present in the ArrayList, it is found in the ArrayList (arrList.Contains(x) == TRUE and for every int i in arrList, Assert.IsTrue(i == x))

This covers the key contracts for ArrayList. It's worth noting that this code is just a part of much larger testing suite and does not represent a complete, fully automated and tested implementation. The purpose is to validate a specific operation in code, in this case the ArrayList Insert method. It's a simple way of testing and demonstrating the idea of PexOS's capacity to prove its contracts about the program under test. Please note this code won't work without the appropriate testing framework and dependencies.

