The assertions failed for the following reasons: The actual result does not satisfy the precondition. The precondition was that index is valid position. Actual value was -4096. It means that the index provided is greater than the maximum valid index (Count of the ArrayList) by 1 units. This is caused by an issue in the assumption/requirement of the test.

To fix this, the assumption for the test should be that index is less than or equal to the Count of the ArrayList (if it is a valid position to insert a new element), or equal to the Count and we should test if the capacity is enough for addition of new elements. For the actual assertions about Count and IndexOf, there should be checking for the case when we are adding element to the end of the ArrayList.

The correct assumption could be as follows:

AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index <= arrList.Count); or AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index == arrList.Count && index + arrList.TrimmedCount == arrList.Capacity)
